# master is the web-only version of this project — android/ and ios/ are
# tracked on feature/capacitor-mobile only (see that branch's own
# .gitignore, which has no such rule). Since .gitignore is itself a
# versioned file, this line only takes effect while checked out on master;
# it exists so switching from feature/capacitor-mobile back here doesn't
# leave those native project dirs cluttering `git status`/`git add -A`
# (checkout doesn't remove them — they're only untracked here, not part of
# master's tree).
/android/
/ios/
